Security Best Practices in GitHub Actions

Today I focused on security practices that help protect CI/CD pipelines from misconfigurations and leaks.

🔹 Least Privilege
Grant workflows:
Only required permissions
Minimal access to resources
Restricted scopes
This reduces blast radius.

🔹 Secret Masking
Secret masking:
Hides sensitive values in logs
Prevents accidental exposure
Automatically applied to secrets
Logs stay safe and clean.

🔹 Action Pinning
Action pinning:
Locks actions to versions or SHAs
Prevents unexpected changes
Improves workflow stability
This protects against supply-chain risks.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Limit permissions.
 Hide secrets.
 Pin dependencies.
